# Environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#   copy .env.example .env.local   (Windows)
#   cp .env.example .env.local     (macOS/Linux)
#
# `.env.local` is ignored by git. Never commit real secrets.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the SQLite database file is stored.
# Optional. Defaults to `.data/tasks.db` inside the project.
# The folder is created automatically and is ignored by git.
#
# This is a local file path, not a secret. If you later point the app at a
# hosted database, keep any credentials in this file and read them in `lib/`
# — never hard-code them in the app.
DATABASE_PATH=".data/tasks.db"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No secrets are required. The database is a local file, so there is nothing
# sensitive to store yet.
#
# When an external service is added, list its variables here with placeholder
# values only, for example:
#
#   # API key for the email service.
#   EMAIL_API_KEY="replace-me"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
